   "text": "I read the structure in four pieces and joined them into one SMILES.\n\n- **Left end:** a 4-methoxybenzyl ether on a 3-methoxy-4-oxy-benzyl group. That benzyl is attached to N3 of a 2-amino-3H-imidazo[4,5-b]pyridine.\n- **Core:** the pyridine carbon at position 6 of the imidazopyridine carries a pyrazol-4-yl group. The pyrazole N1 bears a CH2C(=O)NH linker.\n- **Linker:** NH\u2013CH2CH2 followed by four repeats of O\u2013CH2CH2, where the last repeat leads into C(=O). In SMILES this is NCCOCCOCCOCCOCCC(=O), with four ether oxygens, as drawn.\n- **Right end:** a tert-leucine residue, then a 4-hydroxyproline, then an amide to 4-(4-methylthiazol-5-yl)benzylamine. This is the VHL ligand VH032 pattern.\n\nFor stereochemistry, I took the wedges and hashes on the tert-leucine \u03b1-carbon and on the proline C2 and C4 carbons as the natural VH032 configuration. I wrote each centre in the neighbour order of my own string, and the tags below come from converting the standard VH032 SMILES to that order.\n\nSMILES: COc1ccc(COc2ccc(Cn3c(N)nc4cc(-c5cnn(CC(=O)NCCOCCOCCOCCOCCC(=O)N[C@@H](C(C)(C)C)C(=O)N6C[C@H](O)C[C@H]6C(=O)NCc6ccc(cc6)-c6scnc6C)c5)cnc43)cc2OC)cc1"
